%% Sequence Diagram: Search by Image (CBIR — Model-Agnostic)
%% Based on Chapter 7 — Detailed Design

sequenceDiagram
    actor Customer
    participant StoreSPA as Store SPA<br/>(Vue 3)
    participant Carter as Carter Endpoint<br/>(SearchByImage.Endpoint)
    participant Handler as SearchByImage<br/>QueryHandler
    participant Embedding as Embedding Sidecar<br/>(Python / FastAPI / Strategy Pattern)
    participant Db as ApplicationDbContext<br/>(EF Core + pgvector)
    participant Cache as HybridCache<br/>(L1 Memory / L2 Redis)

    Customer->>StoreSPA: Upload fashion image
    StoreSPA->>Carter: POST /api/admin/catalog/storefront/search-by-image<br/>multipart/form-data
    Carter->>Handler: sender.Send(new Query(imageBytes))

    Handler->>Cache: TryGet(cacheKey: imageHash)
    alt Cache hit
        Cache-->>Handler: Cached results
    else Cache miss
        Handler->>Embedding: POST /embeddings<br/>{image: base64, model: "fashion-clip"}

        Embedding->>Embedding: Model Registry resolves<br/>FashionCLIPModel via EMBEDDING_MODEL
        Embedding->>Embedding: Lazy-load model (if cold start)
        Embedding->>Embedding: Model-specific preprocessing<br/>(resize + normalize per model)
        Embedding->>Embedding: encode_image()<br/>(torch inference)
        Embedding-->>Handler: {embedding: [...], model_name: "fashion-clip", vector_dim: 512}

        Handler->>Db: SELECT vi.*, v.sku, p.name<br/>FROM variant_images vi<br/>JOIN variants v ON ...<br/>JOIN products p ON ...<br/>WHERE vi.model_name = 'fashion-clip'<br/>ORDER BY vi.embedding <=> @embedding<br/>LIMIT 20
        Db-->>Handler: Top-K similar images

        Handler->>Cache: Set(cacheKey, results, 5min)
    end

    Handler-->>Carter: Result<PagedResult<SearchResult>>
    Carter-->>StoreSPA: 200 OK<br/>{products: [...], similarityScores: [...]}
```

## Diagram Description

This sequence illustrates the **Content-Based Image Retrieval (CBIR)** flow with **model-agnostic embedding generation**.

Design decisions:

1. **Strategy Pattern in Sidecar** — The sidecar maintains a registry of `BaseEmbeddingModel` subclasses. The active model is selected at runtime via `EMBEDDING_MODEL` env var or query parameter, enabling the comparative evaluation in Chapter 11.
2. **Model-specific preprocessing** — Each model class encapsulates its own resize/normalize logic (e.g., Fashion-CLIP vs ResNet-50 may differ in interpolation or mean/std).
3. **Per-model database filtering** — The SQL query includes `WHERE model_name = 'fashion-clip'` to ensure only embeddings from the same model are compared. This prevents comparing a Fashion-CLIP query vector against ResNet-50 catalog vectors (different semantic spaces).
4. **HybridCache** — Repeated searches for the same image avoid re-computing the embedding.
5. **Cosine similarity (`<=>`)** — pgvector operator optimized for normalized vectors from any model.

**Evidence**: `ImageEmbedding.Inference.cs:21-36`, `Vector.Configuration.cs`, `service/Embedding/src/services/embedding_service.py`, `ApiTests/Catalog/Storefront/search-by-image.http`
